    "media:imagetext": "Thanks for Atari HOTEL you\nyou\n9 just\nadors it\n- am\ntaking it out now\nMarch 15th\n33\nCATHOTEL\"\nDearest Debs;\nI am really getting very fond of this\nlittle old typewriter, it is easier for me to write\non it than by hand because as you know my arm is\nstill not so good - that is it hurts me a little to\nwrite at much length. So I hope you dont mind this.\nI have just this minute received your\n6th and 7th letters together with one from Bo. What\ndelayed them since yesterday I do not know. Want to\ntake this opportunity to answer some questions in\nyours of the 14th. The ST.L.G.\u0026Q are running true to\nform I fear. Hope you will have ben able to get that\naccount straightened out by this time. Also hope that\nMary Love will be able to get McCurdy to pay the bill\nfor water bur agree with you that we ahould not coll-\nect under the lease if it will jeopardise the lease.\nThe important thing now is to keep the house rented.\nI have not heard yet about the sale of the two acres\nactually being completed and payment received. Hope\nRalph was able to handle that for us.\nPoor Henry he has a real problem with\nKitty. As you say she is just plain poison, and is\ngetting worse all the time.\nThe Income tax matter is\nOK. I should have told you about that but it was one\nof the things I failed to do. The Treasury Dept. was\ntrying to take advantage of a technicality to cheat\nme out of $ 2,000.00 and I think that by filing an\nammended return I will ultimately be able to get some\nmoney back which I have already paid. Your Father's\nauditor fixed up the ammended return for me and it is\njust possible that he may be able to represent my int-\nersts without waiting until 1934. You might send this\nletter, or this part of it to your Father with a re-\nport of what Aud's lawyer wrote for you to the author-\nities in Washington. Re\nRegarding Ralph's assignment to our children\nI wish you would write to the ST.L Union and tell them\nthat you know I do not want that done.\nLots + lots of horr. Bir",
